AND A PORT-ONLY PASS: `restoration::apply_restoration_frame` is 27,076,737
Ir (1.67 %) on photo_cid, 27,076,774 (2.94 %) on the screenshot, 14,704,153
(2.31 %) on the line art and ZERO on the gradient (where no unit selects a
filter). C's profile has NO frame-apply symbol on any of these cells: its
only `svt_av1_loop_restoration_filter_unit` calls (6) are inside
`try_restoration_unit_seg` in the search. This record does NOT claim the
pass is unnecessary — a single-frame still encode needs no filtered
reference, which is the obvious hypothesis, but the C side was not traced to
the point where its recon path is understood, and the port's output is
byte-identical WITH the pass. It is named here as the next thing to read in
C, not as a diagnosed defect.

